context registry.store

uses registry.paths
consumes bynk.cloudflare
consumes bynk.cloudflare { R2, EdgeCache }

---
The registry's bucket, owned by this context alone (standard-library D3): the
read service here, and the publish service and index writers that join it,
are the only code that touches it. Its keys mirror a static registry directory.
---
capability Store = R2

---
Cloudflare's edge cache for this context's Worker (L7, ADR 0613): declaring it
turns Workers Cache on, so a `@cache` route's `2xx` is kept at the edge and
every other `GET` answer is `no-store`. A takedown purges an archive's path
(`operator.bynk`); nothing else purges.
---
capability Edge = EdgeCache

---
The protocol's read paths (`registry-protocol.md`): `config.json`, each
package's index file, and each archive, served as the bytes the bucket holds.
Nothing here signs or decides anything; a client verifies every line and every
archive it reads.

Cached at the edge (R6.1, decisions B and C). `config.json` and the index
files change in place (a delegation, a revocation, a yank, a withdrawal), so
they are kept for 60 seconds at most, and revalidate against their `ETag`.
That is the stated bound on a stale read: purging on every write would run
into the purge rate limit. An archive is content-addressed, so it never
changes: it is `immutable`, with its digest as a strong `ETag`, and only a
takedown purges it. Each route serves every caller alike (`by Visitor`), as a
`public` route in a context with an edge cache must.
---
service files from http {
	@cache(maxAge: 60.seconds, scope: public)
	on GET("/config.json") () -> Effect[HttpResult[()]] by Visitor given Store {
		let found <- Store.get(configKey())
		match found {
			Some(body) => Raw(body, "application/json"),
			None => NotFound,
		}
	}

	@cache(maxAge: 60.seconds, scope: public)
	on GET("/:org/:package") (
		org: String,
		package: String
	) -> Effect[HttpResult[()]] by Visitor given Store {
		match indexKey(org, package) {
			None => NotFound,
			Some(key) => {
				let found <- Store.get(key)
				match found {
					Some(body) => Raw(body, "application/x-ndjson"),
					None => NotFound,
				}
			},
		}
	}

	@cache(maxAge: 365.days, scope: public, immutable: true)
	on GET("/dl/sha256/:hex") (hex: String) -> Effect[HttpResult[()]] by Visitor given Store {
		match archiveKey(hex) {
			None => NotFound,
			Some(key) => {
				let found <- Store.get(key)
				match found {
					Some(body) => RawTagged(body, "application/vnd.bynk.tree-v1", "\"\(hex)\""),
					None => NotFound,
				}
			},
		}
	}
}
